<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03R8">Example <span data-tag="03R8">4.9.2.12</span> <span class="named">(The First Uncountable Cardinal)</span>.</a> We say that a cardinal $\kappa $ is <em>uncountable</em> if it is strictly larger than $\aleph _0$. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="03R5" href="/tag/03R5">4.9.2.9</a>, there is a smallest uncountable cardinal, which we denote by $\aleph _{1}$. In other words, $\aleph _{1}$ is the successor cardinal $\aleph _0^{+}$. </p>
